' S-606 (2026-10-17): `Say.Dort()` names an INSTANCE method through its class. The AST interpreter ran it (printed 4 with no object); MIR,
' native x64, JS, WASM and legacy AST-x64 refused it. Every engine now stops at compile time with the same message.
CLASS Say
    PUBLIC
    METHOD Dort() AS I32
        RETURN 4
    END METHOD
END CLASS
PRINT Say.Dort()
